              <div class="text-slate-900 font-bold text-lg mb-2">Thayngen customs: T1 versus ATA Carnet</div>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-3">Switzerland is not part of the EU Customs Union. Permanent import uses the T1 transit procedure with clearance at the Thayngen customs office and 8.1 per cent Swiss VAT. Temporary rental containers (for example clinical studies) use an ATA Carnet under temporary admission — no VAT, with a security deposit. Standard freight operators do not calculate this.</p>
              <p class="text-xs text-slate-900 font-semibold pt-3 border-t border-gray-200">Planexus standard: T1 or ATA Carnet according to project duration, Thayngen clearance co-ordinated.</p>
